From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PROPOSED] mf: defer sink demand until seek sources restart

Review overlay against the final A3.19 Wine tree, not an integrated patch.
If accepted, fold this correction into patch 0007 in a fresh candidate;
the A3.19 pin, series, sources, and installed artifact remain unchanged.

Running sinks can request another sample while a seek has stopped the
sources and cleared transform demand. WineDMO correctly rejects an inactive
stream's RequestSample(), but the synchronous transform retains its output
request. Later demand sees had_requests and does not restart the pull chain,
including the existing seek-completion re-prime.

Keep the sink's request credit without pulling upstream during the two
source-restart phases. Once every source and selected stream has started,
the existing patch 0007 barrier clears SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING and re-primes
one request per sink. No timer, retry, extra demand, or timeout change is
introduced. Qualify the flag with STARTING_SOURCES so a flag left behind by
a failed start cannot block demand in unrelated session phases.

This closes a source-demonstrable synchronous pull-chain race. The live
episode #331 wrong-state warnings are supporting correlation, not proof
that this is the only cause of its seek stalls. Model tests are not a
Wine runtime or playback result; native/contained and in-game validation
remain required before claiming a fix.

The license of the modified Wine source file applies to this patch.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/session.c b/dlls/mf/session.c
--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -4351,6 +4351,14 @@ static void session_request_sample(struct media_session *session, IMFStreamSink *sink_stream)
     }
 
     sink_node->u.sink.requests++;
+    /* Keep sink demand while stopped seek sources restart. Pulling now can
+     * leave a transform request stranded after MF_E_MEDIA_SOURCE_WRONGSTATE.
+     * The all-sources-started barrier clears RESTARTING before re-priming. */
+    if (session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_RESTARTING_SOURCES
+            || (session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_STARTING_SOURCES
+                && (session->presentation.flags & SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING)))
+        return;
+
     if (FAILED(session_request_sample_from_node(session, up_node, output)))
         sink_node->u.sink.requests--;
 }
